# extend_anim_node_runtime_mapping Design

Date: 2026-06-27
Updated: 2026-06-29

Status: First Tivret diagnostic pass implemented. `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose`
now reports `mapping_support` for dry-run, compiled mapping, and PoseWatch
responses. Node-specific runtime fallback expansion remains design/review work.

Scope: editor-only/runtime-probe support expansion for
`sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose`. Runtime/gameplay code and asset
mutation are out of scope.

## Purpose

`extend_anim_node_runtime_mapping` is an implementation playbook for cases where
an AnimGraph node can be found statically but cannot yet produce same-instance
pre/post pose evidence.

The goal is to reduce failures when a user selects a node class outside the
current proven set. The extension should improve mapping diagnostics and, only
when evidence is strong enough, allow `pose_watch_capture` to report
`runtime_graph_prepost=true` and `same_instance_prepost=true`.

## Ieta Review

Request class: prove one selected AnimGraph node changed pose output, but the
current resolver, runtime node mapping, runtime pose-link inventory, or
PoseWatch capture cannot attribute the selected node.

Existing routes checked:

- `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose(dry_run=true)` resolves the editor
  graph, target node, preferred pins, settings, and static links.
- `mode=compiled_graph_mapping` maps the editor node GUID to generated-class
  `FAnimNode_*` property data and a live AnimInstance node pointer.
- `mode=pose_watch_capture` registers transient debug PoseWatch entries for the
  selected runtime node output and selected input pose link IDs.
- `mode=active_component_tick_delta` samples only final component pose deltas.
- `mode=isolated_temp_components` can compare temp source-vs-output assets for
  supported fixture-style nodes.

Why existing routes may be insufficient: some node classes do not expose a
simple runtime `FPoseLink`/`FComponentSpacePoseLink` input, hide their useful
input in nested arrays, evaluate conditionally, or are source/sink nodes where
pre/post attribution is not meaningful.

Asset mutation boundary: mapping and PoseWatch work must be runtime-only or
read-only. Isolated temp comparison may create only `_MCP_Temp` assets through
the existing mode.

Proposed candidate: extend existing `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose`
internals, not a new user-facing command by default.

Approval status: user approved the Ieta/Tivret plan for the first diagnostic
C++/API pass on 2026-06-29. Further node-specific fallbacks, new commands, or
asset mutation still require Ieta review.

## Current Implementation Anchors

Use these existing paths first:

| Existing function/path | Current role |
| --- | --- |
| `AnimGraphCompiledNodeMappingToJson` | Maps editor `NodeGuid` to generated-class node index, `FStructProperty`, runtime node pointer, and `FindDebugAnimNode`. |
| `RuntimeAnimNodePoseLinksToJson` | Recursively inventories runtime `FPoseLinkBase` fields on the live `FAnimNode_*` struct. |
| `CollectRuntimePoseLinksFromStruct` | Walks nested structs and arrays up to `pose_link_max_depth`. |
| `SelectRuntimePoseLinksForPoseWatch` | Chooses `input_pose_field_path`, `input_pose_index`, `first`, or `all`. |
| `RegisterTransientAnimPoseWatch` | Adds transient debug-data PoseWatch entries without saving the AnimBP asset. |
| `CaptureAnimNodePoseWatchPose` | Reads PoseWatch bone transforms after controlled ticks. |
| `GetAnimNodePrePostMVPKind` | Current coarse support label for a few study node classes. |
| `Docs/Tools/node_tools.md` | Public schema and evidence wording for `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose`. |

## UE 5.6 API Anchors

| Need | UE 5.6 anchor | Safe access rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Generated class mapping | `Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimBlueprintGeneratedClass.h` | Use `GetNodeIndexFromGuid()`, `GetAnimNodeProperties()`, and visual-node mapping helpers. |
| Runtime node base | `Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimNodeBase.h` | Require mapped structs to derive from `FAnimNode_Base`. |
| Runtime pose links | `Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimNodeBase.h` | Discover `FPoseLinkBase`, `FPoseLink`, and `FComponentSpacePoseLink` fields by reflection. |
| Runtime AnimInstance | `Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimInstance.h` | Match a live AnimInstance compatible with the target AnimBP class. |
| Editor node mapping | `Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimGraphNode_Base.h` | Use editor node GUIDs and `FindDebugAnimNode()`. |
| PoseWatch debug data | `Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimBlueprintGeneratedClass.h` and `Engine/PoseWatch.h` | Register transient entries only; restore debug object and remove transient watches. |

## Support Classification

Classify a selected node before claiming proof:

| Class | Criteria | Allowed evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `static_only` | Node resolves statically but no compatible live AnimInstance exists. | Topology/settings only. |
| `compiled_mapping_only` | `GetNodeIndexFromGuid()` and runtime pointer mapping succeed, but no valid runtime pose input link exists. | Same-instance mapping, not pre/post pose. |
| `output_only_source_node` | Asset players or source nodes have no meaningful upstream pose input. | Output PoseWatch or final-pose evidence, not source-vs-output attribution. |
| `single_input_pose_node` | One valid runtime pose link maps to an upstream node. | PoseWatch pre/post can be supported. |
| `multi_input_pose_node` | Multiple valid pose links exist in arrays or nested structs. | PoseWatch with `input_pose_mode=all` or exact `input_pose_field_path`. |
| `component_space_pose_node` | Runtime input uses component-space pose link fields. | PoseWatch can be supported only if captured transforms are valid. |
| `conditional_or_latent_node` | Link exists but may not evaluate every tick. | Require warning and controlled tick/settle evidence. |
| `unsupported_for_prepost` | Sink, transition result, state machine, linked layer boundary, or node lacks stable pose link semantics. | Do not report `same_instance_prepost=true`. |

## Extension Criteria

A node class can be promoted to PoseWatch-supported only when all are true:

- target selection is unambiguous by `node_id` or strict filters;
- generated-class node index is found from the editor `NodeGuid`;
- mapped `FStructProperty` derives from `FAnimNode_Base`;
- live AnimInstance class is compatible with the resolved AnimBP class;
- runtime node pointer or `FindDebugAnimNode()` mapping succeeds;
- at least one runtime pose link has a valid `link_id`;
- selected pre input link and post output link both register transient
  PoseWatches;
- after settle/tick, both watches capture transforms from the same expected
  AnimInstance;
- debug object is restored and transient PoseWatches are removed;
- response keeps evidence labels honest.

If any condition fails, return a structured diagnostic and keep
`runtime_graph_prepost=false`.

## Implemented Diagnostic Pass

The first implementation keeps the existing command surface and adds no asset
mutation:

- `target_node.mapping_support` is available during dry-run/static resolution;
- `compiled_graph_mapping` returns top-level `mapping_support` after live
  generated-class node mapping and runtime pose-link inventory;
- `pose_watch_capture` returns top-level `mapping_support`, using
  `evidence_tier=same_instance_pose_watch` only when pre/post PoseWatch capture
  succeeds;
- `support_class` can report `static_only`, `compiled_mapping_only`,
  `output_only_source_node`, `single_input_pose_node`, `multi_input_pose_node`,
  `component_space_pose_node`, or `unsupported_for_prepost`;
- source/sink/boundary nodes keep `pose_watch_supported=false` so lower evidence
  is not overstated as selected-node pre/post proof.

## Preferred Future Design Change

Implement as an extension to `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose`:

- add a support matrix in code or docs keyed by editor class name and runtime
  struct name;
- record preferred input field paths for known multi-input nodes;
- keep dry-run output populated with `mapping_support.support_class`,
  `recommended_input_pose_mode`, `known_good_field_paths`, and
  `unsupported_reason`;
- keep `input_pose_field_path` as the override for user-selected links;
- keep generic recursive `FPoseLinkBase` discovery as the first path before any
  node-specific fallback;
- add node-specific fallbacks only when generic reflection cannot expose a
  stable link path.

Do not add persistent project settings or a data asset for the support matrix in
the first implementation. Keep it in the editor-only bridge code and docs until
the pattern stabilizes.

## Response Additions

Current `mapping_support` fields:

```json
{
  "mapping_support": {
    "node_class": "",
    "runtime_struct": "",
    "support_class": "single_input_pose_node",
    "pose_watch_supported": true,
    "recommended_mode": "pose_watch_capture",
    "recommended_input_pose_mode": "all",
    "known_good_field_paths": [],
    "unsupported_reason": "",
    "evidence_tier": "same_instance_pose_watch",
    "valid_runtime_pose_link_count": 1,
    "runtime_pose_links_checked": true,
    "runtime_node_instance_mapped": true,
    "find_debug_anim_node_mapped": true,
    "same_anim_instance_node_mapping": true
  }
}
```

Evidence tiers:

- `static_topology`
- `compiled_node_mapping`
- `runtime_pose_link_inventory`
- `same_instance_pose_watch`
- `final_component_tick_delta`
- `isolated_temp_comparison`

Only `same_instance_pose_watch` may set both `runtime_graph_prepost=true` and
`same_instance_prepost=true`.

## Forbidden Patterns

Do not use these in implementation:

- hardcoding runtime `LinkID` numbers from one compiled class;
- assuming editor pin order equals runtime pose-link field order;
- claiming node attribution from `active_component_tick_delta`;
- leaving the AnimBP debug object changed;
- adding persistent PoseWatches to the AnimBP asset;
- saving assets during mapping or PoseWatch capture;
- increasing recursive struct traversal without hard limits;
- treating source nodes as source-vs-output pre/post nodes;
- swallowing PoseWatch capture failures while still reporting success;
- using Unreal Python generated-class property guesses instead of C++ mapping.

Reason: these patterns make evidence unstable, mutate editor state, or overstate
what the probe actually proved.

## Verification Plan

For docs-only changes:

```powershell
git diff --check
```

For implementation:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\node_tools.py
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
```

For read-only bridge smoke of the implemented diagnostic:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_anim_node_mapping_support_bridge.py --json
```

This smoke uses the engine Tutorial AnimBP root node as an unsupported pre/post
fixture and confirms `mapping_support.support_class=unsupported_for_prepost`,
`pose_watch_supported=false`, and `evidence_tier=static_topology`.

When no Unreal Editor bridge is already running, use the launcher wrapper:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\run_anim_node_mapping_support_smoke.ps1 -Json
```

Editor smoke verification after implementation should:

- run `dry_run=true` for one known supported node and one unsupported node;
- run `mode=compiled_graph_mapping` on a live compatible component;
- run `mode=pose_watch_capture` with `input_pose_mode=first`;
- run `mode=pose_watch_capture` with `input_pose_mode=all` on a multi-input
  node;
- confirm unsupported/source nodes keep `same_instance_prepost=false`;
- confirm no AnimBP asset gets new persistent PoseWatch objects;
- confirm debug object restoration after success and failure;
- confirm response evidence tier matches the actual mode.

## Tivret instruction

Do not add node-specific fallbacks, a new command, or asset mutation from this
document unless a concrete selected node class fails the existing
resolver/mapping/PoseWatch path and the active request explicitly moves to that
implementation. When approved:

- target files: likely
  `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/Commands/UnrealMCPBlueprintNodeCommands.cpp`,
  matching public declaration header if needed, `Python/tools/node_tools.py`,
  and `Docs/Tools/node_tools.md`;
- extend existing `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose` rather than adding a
  parallel proof command;
- keep runtime probe code editor-only and non-saving;
- add diagnostics before adding node-specific fallbacks;
- update docs with exact evidence labels and limitations;
- rollback boundary: remove the new mapping support and docs entry only; do not
  revert unrelated docs or user changes.
